   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1942-02-14">Febr. 14. 1942</date>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__931" type="person">Dr. Max Horkheimer</rs>
               13524 d´Este Drive
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__851" type="place">Pacific Palisade, Cal.</rs></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__931" type="person">Horkheimer</rs> :</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I enclose a letter about <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__106" type="person">Julius Bab</rs>. He was in my office about a year ago
               and made a very fine and even unforgettable impression on me. Since that time I did not hear anything about him. <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3339" 
                  type="person">Mrs. Frankel</rs> to whom I dictate this letter tells me that <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3487">Mrs. Bab</rs> looks like a 
            very old and sick woman but that the National  Refugee Service declines to help them because they have a 
            son<!-- laut Wikipedia hatte Julius Bab einen Sohn namens Björn --> who refuses to support his parents.</p>
            <p>The only idea which came to my mind was to ask you whether Hollywood could help to publish such a work which would be of extreme interest
               for everybody who have to do with theater or movie. Would you be so good to discuss the situation with <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3488"
            type="person">Dieterle</rs> or somebody who would help to dimin<del>u</del>ish a little bit the misery in which the 
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__106" type="person"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3487">Bab</rs></rs>´s live.</p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Very cordially yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                  ><add hand="#tillich_person_id__1928">Paul Tillich</add> Prof. Paul Tillich</rs></signed>
            </closer>
            <postscript><p>encl.</p></postscript>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
